  "content": "Month-long Adinath Mela begins in Chobhar\nOnlinekhabar\nTuesday, October 7, 2025\n0\nComments\nKathmandu, October 7\nA month-long Mela (fair) has begun at the Adinath Temple located on Chobhar Hill in Kathmandu. The Adinath Mela starts on the day of Kojagrat Purnima and continues until Kartik Shukla Purnima.\nDevotees throng the temple to worship the combined image of Lord Shiva and Goddess Parvati, known as Ardhanarishwar Adinath. It is believed that participating in the Mela brings freedom from fear, disease, and obstacles, and bestows happiness and prosperity upon families.\nThe Adinath Temple is revered by both Hindu and Buddhist devotees as a shared place of worship. Believed to have been established during the Lichhavi period by King Amsuvarma, the temple holds great historical and archaeological significance.\nBuddhist followers worship Adinath as Lokeshwar, believing that doing so grants longevity, protection from untimely death, and material prosperity. Hindus, on the other hand, worship Adinath as a manifestation of Shiva and Shakti.\nSituated about nine kilometres south of Kathmandu, the temple offers a scenic view of the Kathmandu Valley from Chobhar Hill. Nearby religious sites of significance include Manjushree Park, Jal Binayak Temple, and Taudaha Lake.\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\nNepal\nElection Commission\ncricket\nshare market\nroad\nGen Z\nMaitighar\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nWhat’s behind the controversy at Chobhar Gorge?\n3 months ago\nMonth-long fair kicks off in Chobhar Adinath\n12 months ago\nMost Read\nHighways blocked nationwide as heavy rainfall disrupts travel\nFlood risks in Kathmandu, KMC launches helpline service\nUAE introduces new rules for Visit Visa Sponsorship\nCAA publishes domestic airfare rates, Kathmandu–Dhangadhi at Rs 17,579\nDeath toll from landslides and floods rises to 52 across Nepal\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nSubscribe to Onlinekhabar English to get notified of exclusive news stories.\nEditor's Pick\nEditor's Pick\n4 government buildings, including Supreme Court, declared unfit for use\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nCharred body found at Koteshwor Bhatbhateni, Gen-Z protest death toll rises to 74\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nNo consensus on Hami Nepal’s claim of leading the Gen-Z movement\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nDecades-old irrigation projects stall as Madhesh faces drought, food crisis looms\n3 months ago\nEditor's Pick\nNepal’s farming crisis: When plans stay on paper and fields suffer\n3 months ago\nAlso Read\nOpinion\nGen Z movement in Nepal at a crossroads: Between reform, revolt and reflection\n9 hours ago\nSociety\nDiversions built at 3 sections of BP Highway\n9 hours ago\nBlog\nHow Gen Z turned a hashtag into a revolution in Nepal\n9 hours ago\nPolitics\nElection Commission invites parties for talks on upcoming House election\n1 day ago\nSociety\nSeven charged in Pokhara Lichhibari land scam involving former ministers and officials\n1 day ago",
